## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a practical KCA workflow for IoT scale with policy binding, offline revocation, and streaming updates in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts

- CSR enrollment and short-lived TLS certs
- SPIFFE ID binding per district
- Per-district policy binding and streaming updates
- Offline revocation with local CRLs
- Auditing and device-scale testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: enrollment flow sketch
async function enrollSensor(sensor, district) {
  const attestation = regionalBootstrap.attest(sensor);
  const csr = sensor.createCSR(district);
  const cert = centralKCA.issue cert({ csr, ttl: 600-900, spiffe: `spiffe://city/${district}/iot` });
  sensor.store(cert);
  // subscribe to policy stream
  policyServer.subscribe(sensor, district);
}
```

